1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,720
It is weird even for me because when I was younger there was so much pressure to be the best in everything.
连她自己也觉得奇怪，因为小时候，她面临巨大压力，什么都要做到最好。

2
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:08,321
To never make mistakes that I didn't have any room to breathe.
还不能犯错，以至于她连喘息的空间都没有。

3
00:00:08,321 --> 00:00:13,681
I also had a lot of cousins around and never had even a moment to myself.
她身边还有很多表兄弟姐妹，从来没有哪怕片刻能自己待着。

4
00:00:13,681 --> 00:00:20,391
As an introvert that was completely suffocating and I preferred being in boarding school.
作为内向的人，那完全让她喘不过气；她反而更愿意住寄宿学校。

5
00:00:20,401 --> 00:00:26,161
However the memory of such experiences leaves such a bad taste in the mouth and also lots of trauma.
然而，这些经历的记忆留下很糟的感受，也带来许多创伤。

6
00:00:26,161 --> 00:00:31,031
Not because of those experiences per se really because of the loneliness that came with them.
她说，原因并不在那些经历本身，而在于伴随它们的孤独。

7
00:00:31,041 --> 00:00:35,201
You had to do things you didn't want because you were being compared to someone else.
你不得不做自己不想做的事，因为总有人拿你和别人比较。

8
00:00:35,201 --> 00:00:39,920
Which meant that nobody really cared to think about what you wanted with your own life.
这意味着，没有人真正关心你希望怎样过自己的人生。

9
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:46,321
You were pushed to live a life you didn't want because it made your parents happy but what about you you're a human being too.
你被推着过自己不想过的人生，只为了让父母高兴。可你呢？你也是人。

10
00:00:46,321 --> 00:00:52,720
Why do parents feel so entitled to the lives of their own children and go as far as not treating them as human beings.
她质问，父母为什么觉得自己理应支配孩子的人生，甚至不把他们当人看？

11
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:57,201
This is the consequence of people having children and not wanting to actually be parents.
她认为，这是有人生了孩子，却不愿真正承担为人父母责任的后果。

12
00:00:57,201 --> 00:01:05,280
They had children to show society their success to create their legacy to create their minimies as an investment for their old age.
她说，他们生孩子，是为了向社会展示成功、延续自身，制造“小号自己”，给晚年投资。〔minimies 识别待复核〕

13
00:01:05,280 --> 00:01:10,080
Parents who forced their children to leave the lives they write are the people who shouldn't have children.
她说，强迫孩子去过他们写好的人生的父母，不应该生孩子。〔leave the lives they write 原字幕疑点，按语境译意，待复核〕

14
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:12,481
And they should just have lived however they wanted.
她认为，他们本该按自己的意愿生活。

15
00:01:12,481 --> 00:01:18,151
No one forced you to have children instead of traveling you do so so that you can belong to the status quo.
没人强迫你生孩子；你没有去旅行，而是为了迎合现状与主流而这样做。

16
00:01:18,161 --> 00:01:22,241
But your children have to pay the cost of living lonely lives just so that.
可你的孩子要付出代价，过着孤独的生活，只是为了——

17
00:01:22,241 --> 00:01:27,521
You can have a semblance of happiness which never really comes because you're always going to be chasing it.
让你获得一种看似幸福的状态，而它永远不会真正到来，因为你会一直追逐它。

18
00:01:27,521 --> 00:01:31,750
So imagine you grew up in a home where emotional abandonment and loneliness was normal.
那么，想象你成长在一个情感忽视和孤独被视为常态的家庭。

19
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:36,001
How do you think you're going to manage your relationships whether friendships or romantic.
你觉得自己会怎样经营人际关系，无论友情还是爱情？

20
00:01:36,001 --> 00:01:40,081
The popular phrase what do you bring to the table is the best symptom of this.
她认为，流行的“你能给这段关系带来什么”这句话，最能体现这一问题。

21
00:01:40,081 --> 00:01:45,911
And if you want healthy relationships run away from anyone that says this on the first day you meet.
她说，如果想要健康的关系，就远离那些初次见面便这样问你的人。

22
00:01:45,921 --> 00:01:51,841
Because they're basically telling you they are so disconnected from their own emotions that they don't know how to be human.
她觉得，那等于在说，他们与自己的情绪脱节到不知道如何作为人相处。

23
00:01:51,841 --> 00:01:58,641
And actually this is a lot of people when you treat yourself like a human being you'll be called boring because yes healthy is.
而她觉得，这样的人很多；当你像对待人一样对待自己，可能被叫作无聊，因为，是的，健康的状态——

24
00:01:58,641 --> 00:02:00,801
Most times just very boring.
大多数时候就是很平淡。

25
00:02:00,801 --> 00:02:08,561
Loneliness breeds a lot of chaos and anxiety emotional outbursts jealousy tantrums all of these are signs of loneliness.
她说，孤独滋生混乱和焦虑；情绪爆发、嫉妒、发脾气，在她看来都是孤独的迹象。

26
00:02:08,561 --> 00:02:14,231
What kind of relationships are you going to have when you don't even realize that you have this kind of emotional loneliness.
如果你都没有意识到自己的这种情感孤独，又会建立怎样的关系呢？

27
00:02:14,241 --> 00:02:17,760
You'll be sewing seeds of chaos and self sabotage over and over.
你会不断种下混乱和自我破坏的种子。〔sewing seeds 原字幕疑似识别，待复核〕

28
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:20,801
You'll repeat the lives of parents you wish to run away from.
你会重复父母那种你想逃离的生活。

29
00:02:20,801 --> 00:02:29,271
And one day you look in the mirror and you realize you have become the kind of person you always wanted to run away from.
某天照镜子，你会发现自己成了那个一直想远离的人。

30
00:02:29,281 --> 00:02:34,081
And so how do you deal with it I believe the antidote is really fast being okay with who you are.
那么该怎样应对？她认为，解药是先接纳自己。〔really fast 原字幕疑点，待听辨〕

31
00:02:34,081 --> 00:02:40,160
And knowing that forcing yourself to be around people that don't care to see nor understand you is not going to help you in any way.
并且明白，强迫自己待在不愿看见、理解你的人身边，不会以任何方式帮到你。

32
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:45,671
Second you have to learn to feel feeling makes you realize how precious fragile and human you are.
第二，要学会感受。感受让你意识到，自己多么珍贵、脆弱，也是一个人。

33
00:02:45,681 --> 00:02:48,241
Feeling is the first step of acknowledging that you are alive.
感受，是承认自己活着的第一步。

34
00:02:48,241 --> 00:02:53,201
And once you know this you realize how gentle you need to be to yourself and in so doing.
一旦明白这一点，你会知道该多么温柔地对待自己；这样做时——

35
00:02:53,201 --> 00:02:58,561
You will attract people who treat you as a human being instead of those addicted to chaos.
你会吸引那些把你当人对待的人，而非沉迷于混乱的人。

36
00:02:58,561 --> 00:03:02,481
Thirdly and the most important you have to define what you want from other people.
第三，也是最重要的，明确你希望从别人那里得到什么。

37
00:03:02,481 --> 00:03:05,121
I know that sometimes you have expectations based on nothing.
她说，有时你对人有期待，却没有相应依据。

38
00:03:05,121 --> 00:03:10,081
And if you don't communicate to those around you about how you expect them to treat you you will be lonely.
如果你不向身边的人说明自己希望被怎样对待，你会感到孤独。

39
00:03:10,081 --> 00:03:15,361
You need to start being proactive about communicating instead of assuming the people around you will just get it.
你需要主动沟通，而不是假设身边的人自然就会明白。

40
00:03:15,361 --> 00:03:22,561
This also means learning to stand up for yourself in your own home to your own parents instead of resenting them when they don't even know what they did wrong.
这也意味着在自己家里、面对父母时为自己发声，而不是在他们甚至不知道错在哪里时一味怨恨。

41
00:03:22,561 --> 00:03:28,801
And of course it is of no use trying to get an apology from people who deny the bad things that they have done.
当然，试图让否认自己做过坏事的人道歉，是没有用的。

42
00:03:28,801 --> 00:03:31,671
It is not your job to make them understand where you're coming from.
让他们理解你的立场，不是你的责任。

43
00:03:31,681 --> 00:03:37,911
Your job is simply to communicate how they made you feel communicate your boundaries and leave your own life.
你的责任只是说明他们让你有何感受，沟通你的边界，再过自己的生活。〔leave your own life 字幕待复核〕

44
00:03:37,921 --> 00:03:41,760
Those who want to remain in your life will make amends and try to meet you halfway.
想留在你生活中的人会弥补过错，尝试与你各让一步。

45
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:48,081
Those that don't care about you they'll simply call you too much crazy or they'll tell you who do you think you are.
而不在乎你的人，只会说你太难应付、疯了，或者问：你以为你是谁？
